# Evidence — the deploy path no longer has to run as cluster-admin (결정 5, 옵션 B)

Date: 2026-07-31 · gate 1584 (1572 -> 1584, +12)
Cluster: kind platform-agent (3 nodes, v1.34.0) — LIVE
Brief: docs/plans/2026-07-30-deploy-request-tenant-scoping.md (추천 B 먼저 -> A)

## 1. Live: render the identity, mint it, and ask the same questions

Both halves are asserted. An identity that is restricted but cannot deploy is
not a fix, it is an outage; an identity that deploys but kept the dangerous
verbs is the status quo with extra YAML.

```

==============================================================================
0. BEFORE — what the ambient credential (today's deploy identity) can do
==============================================================================
    whoami: kubernetes-admin
    ambient can-i get secrets -A                   : yes
    ambient can-i delete namespaces -A             : yes
    ambient can-i create clusterrolebindings       : yes

==============================================================================
1. Render + apply the deploy identity
==============================================================================
    namespace/platform-agent-system created
    serviceaccount/platform-agent-deployer created
    clusterrole.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/platform-agent-deployer created
    clusterrolebinding.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/platform-agent-deployer created

==============================================================================
2. Mint a short-lived kubeconfig for it
==============================================================================
    wrote /tmp/deploy-probe.kubeconfig (valid 20m)
      export PLATFORM_DEPLOY_KUBECONFIG=/tmp/deploy-probe.kubeconfig
    whoami: system:serviceaccount:platform-agent-system:platform-agent-deployer

==============================================================================
3. AFTER — the same questions, asked as the deployer
==============================================================================
    ✓ can-i get secrets -A = no
    ✓ can-i delete namespaces -A = no
    ✓ can-i create namespaces = no
    ✓ can-i create clusterrolebindings = no
    ✓ can-i get nodes = no
    ✓ can-i delete deployments -A = no
    -- and what it still needs:
    ✓ can-i create deployments -A = yes
    ✓ can-i patch deployments -A = yes
    ✓ can-i create services -A = yes
    ✓ can-i get pods -A = yes

==============================================================================
4. A REAL deploy through the real adapter, pinned to that credential
==============================================================================
    deploy_to_cluster(nginx:1.27-alpine) -> status=success error=
    deploy_to_cluster(nginx:1.28-alpine) -> status=success error=
    ✓ live image after two deploys = nginx:1.28-alpine

==============================================================================
5. A REAL rollback through the same credential
==============================================================================
    rollback_deployment -> success=True error=
    ✓ live image after rollback = nginx:1.27-alpine

==============================================================================
6. The reduction is real — try the dangerous thing through the same credential
==============================================================================
    $ kubectl --kubeconfig <deployer> get secrets -n kube-system
      Error from server (Forbidden): secrets is forbidden: User "system:serviceaccount:platform-agent-system:platform-agent-deployer" cannot list resource "secrets" in API group "" in the namespace "kube-system"
    ✓ Forbidden — the API server refused, not our code

==============================================================================
RESULT
==============================================================================
  ALL LIVE ASSERTIONS HELD
```

